From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] init.rc: no flash_recovery service on a device with no recovery

AOSP's init.rc starts /system/bin/install-recovery.sh at every boot, as a
oneshot in class main. That script is generated only for a product that builds
a recovery image, to write the recovery partition again after a system update.
This device builds none: BoardConfig.mk sets TARGET_NO_RECOVERY, the Kindle's
own recovery is Amazon's and this project never writes a partition.

So the file is never there, init fails to start the service, and says so at
every boot. The line looks like a fault and is not one, which is the kind of
log noise that costs somebody an afternoon.

--- a/rootdir/init.rc
+++ b/rootdir/init.rc
@@ -732,7 +732,3 @@
     # The folder is used to store method traces.
     chmod 0773 /data/misc/trace
     start console
-
-service flash_recovery /system/bin/install-recovery.sh
-    class main
-    oneshot
